From f089213479dc30ecc0ea70eec723a611ddb78dbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:42:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 105/638] [AROS] Add a native socket IO message pump

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-2-3
AI_STATUS: in-progress
ROOT_CAUSE: AROS posixc select() is a return-0 stub, and PIPE: does not implement the F_SETFL nonblocking contract required by libevent wakeup pipes.
FIX_REASON: Use AROSTCP WaitSelect() for socket readiness and an Exec signal for cross-task scheduler wakeups, keeping both waits native and atomic.
SCOPE: base/BUILD.gn; base/message_loop/message_pump_aros.{cc,h}; base/message_loop/message_pump_for_io.h
VALIDATION: GN regeneration passed; message_pump_aros.o, message_pump.o, and current_thread.o cross-compiled for pc-x86_64-smp AROS.
RISK: The initial AROS IO pump intentionally watches AROSTCP socket descriptors only; non-socket descriptors require a future native handler/message-port adapter.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: libevent pipe wakeup -> PIPE: nonblocking rejection -> posixc select stub -> native WaitSelect plus Exec signal pump
Continues: def84d9cb5
